[[:db/retract 17592186161378 :answer-field/choices 17592186161379] [:db/retract 17592186161378 :answer-field/choices 17592186161380] [:db/retract 17592186161378 :answer-field/choices 17592186161381] [:db/retract 17592186161378 :answer-field/choices 17592186161382] [:db/retract 17592186161378 :answer-field/choices 17592186161383] {:db/id 17592186162025 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-39bb09ec-48b5-5f33-adde-628ba380f524" "question-14e23c62-ff8b-573c-9dad-c31829390556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161817 :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in \\mathbb Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X = -1)$ can be approximated as $P(a\\leq Y \\leq b).$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We construct an interval around $X=-1$ with a radius of $0.5{:}$\n\n![](images/e9/e92a0fb229125f6a9cd27c96629cd1851f3356ece0bca6aa77b8393f7a0dfd90.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-1) & ≈P(-1-0.5\\le Y\\le -1+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-1.5\\le Y\\le -0.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1.5$ and $b=-0.5.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162026 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a5c8fffc-11c1-576d-8ffb-d7561ffc582e" "question-acbfdb28-97bf-5853-92f1-7b02234a722c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161818 :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in \\mathbb  Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(-1 \\lt X \\lt 2)$ can be approximated as $P(a\\leq Y \\leq b).$ Find the values of $a$ and $b.$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities using non-strict inequalities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1<X<2) & =P(0\\le X\\le 1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $0 \\leq X \\leq 1$ by $0.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le 1) & ≈P(0-0.5\\le Y\\le 1+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-0.5\\le Y\\le 1.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-0.5$ and $b=1.5.$\n\n![](images/52/52e5ddb2af86cba41ad9b05001e6a8720b973492f4cf5239031b972c5bcf2afb.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162027 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c629c32e-40e8-52bc-a310-6147fcdaffe0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161819 :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in \\mathbb Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X > 5)$ can be approximated as $P(Y\\geq a).$ Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities using non-strict inequalities, as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X > 5) =P(X \\geq 6)\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $X \\geq 6$ by $0.5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & ≈P(Y\\ge 6-0.5) \\\\  & =P(Y\\ge 5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=5.5.$\n\n![](images/4b/4b6c945ad08ff50b4d306e1952947cb55d5a05899e91f254f3dde3edde9f6523.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-39bb09ec-48b5-5f33-adde-628ba380f524" :question/id #uuid "39bb09ec-48b5-5f33-adde-628ba380f524" :question/math-academy-id "q-96575" :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=-6)$ can be approximated as" :question/worked-solution "We construct an interval around $X=-6$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](images/9f/9f21d7fe3ba1f4efa7b4e24e3d096d84825ff3712f5854c76dabccf0477f503c.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=-6) & ≈P(-6-0.5\\le Y\\le -6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(-6.5\\le Y\\le -5.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a6b743bc-d9c8-56fe-8d5e-f7334892b2c2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a6b743bc-d9c8-56fe-8d5e-f7334892b2c2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a6b743bc-d9c8-56fe-8d5e-f7334892b2c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dbf5b6ea-b43d-5f57-aefc-8ec56c32af9f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c22abeff-6519-5c1c-b37c-17d8868df498" "answer-dbf5b6ea-b43d-5f57-aefc-8ec56c32af9f" "answer-c57399ae-8b01-53a4-8e86-b563135edb9d" "answer-5aaa8fbe-c71d-5ef9-bcf8-eda3e50e0a7e" "answer-306fb1b6-2208-5ab0-aa7a-47a347222ea8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c22abeff-6519-5c1c-b37c-17d8868df498" :answer/id #uuid "c22abeff-6519-5c1c-b37c-17d8868df498" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(-6.5\\le Y\\le -5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbf5b6ea-b43d-5f57-aefc-8ec56c32af9f" :answer/id #uuid "dbf5b6ea-b43d-5f57-aefc-8ec56c32af9f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(-6.5\\le Y\\le -5.5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c57399ae-8b01-53a4-8e86-b563135edb9d" :answer/id #uuid "c57399ae-8b01-53a4-8e86-b563135edb9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(-6\\le Y\\le -5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5aaa8fbe-c71d-5ef9-bcf8-eda3e50e0a7e" :answer/id #uuid "5aaa8fbe-c71d-5ef9-bcf8-eda3e50e0a7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(-6\\le Y\\le -5.5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-306fb1b6-2208-5ab0-aa7a-47a347222ea8" :answer/id #uuid "306fb1b6-2208-5ab0-aa7a-47a347222ea8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(-7\\le Y\\le -6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-14e23c62-ff8b-573c-9dad-c31829390556" :question/id #uuid "14e23c62-ff8b-573c-9dad-c31829390556" :question/math-academy-id "q-132216" :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(X=1)$ can be approximated as" :question/worked-solution "We construct an interval around $X=1$ with a radius of $0.5:$\n\n![](images/51/511cbc0773dab19fe30f555dd3bb1389714ea46ff3748e06026aeb36521ab9d9.png)\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=1) & ≈P(1-0.5\\le Y\\le 1+0.5) \\\\  & =P(0.5\\le Y\\le 1.5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2df7071f-9380-5e73-ad2a-5d2bc94f98a6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2df7071f-9380-5e73-ad2a-5d2bc94f98a6" :answer-field/id #uuid "2df7071f-9380-5e73-ad2a-5d2bc94f98a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-730ec8c9-b1ba-5ef7-b7a0-cf386b5801f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aa790759-a84c-5267-90b9-4ef054bbd799" "answer-730ec8c9-b1ba-5ef7-b7a0-cf386b5801f4" "answer-6d131e3a-6efe-55af-a238-5ce21e629512" "answer-84cfca12-8f4d-5237-a655-33a9336f0b4d" "answer-9b250ce1-4a22-566b-9377-11bfb1748f72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa790759-a84c-5267-90b9-4ef054bbd799" :answer/id #uuid "aa790759-a84c-5267-90b9-4ef054bbd799" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(0.5\\le Y\\le 1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-730ec8c9-b1ba-5ef7-b7a0-cf386b5801f4" :answer/id #uuid "730ec8c9-b1ba-5ef7-b7a0-cf386b5801f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(0.5\\le Y\\le 1.5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d131e3a-6efe-55af-a238-5ce21e629512" :answer/id #uuid "6d131e3a-6efe-55af-a238-5ce21e629512" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(0\\le Y\\le 1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84cfca12-8f4d-5237-a655-33a9336f0b4d" :answer/id #uuid "84cfca12-8f4d-5237-a655-33a9336f0b4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(1\\le Y\\le 1.5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b250ce1-4a22-566b-9377-11bfb1748f72" :answer/id #uuid "9b250ce1-4a22-566b-9377-11bfb1748f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(1\\le Y\\le 2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a5c8fffc-11c1-576d-8ffb-d7561ffc582e" :question/id #uuid "a5c8fffc-11c1-576d-8ffb-d7561ffc582e" :question/math-academy-id "q-96643" :question/problem "The discrete random variable $X\\in Z$ can be approximated by the continuous random variable $Y.$ By applying an appropriate continuity correction, $P(2<X<7)$ can be approximated as" :question/worked-solution "To apply the appropriate continuity correction, we first rewrite the strict inequalities as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<7) & =P(3\\le X\\le 6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we extend the endpoints of the interval $3\\le X\\le 6$ by $0.5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3\\le X\\le 6) & ≈P(3-0.5\\le Y\\le 6+0.5) \\\\  & =P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-50791223-ab5f-58cd-9a39-6290ec407274"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-50791223-ab5f-58cd-9a39-6290ec407274" :answer-field/id #uuid "50791223-ab5f-58cd-9a39-6290ec407274" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-af7e026a-25c7-5309-a590-6ae712847280" :answer-field/choices ["answer-90a38e10-7f75-5d58-827d-ea0f8b66ba3d" "answer-af7e026a-25c7-5309-a590-6ae712847280" "answer-bc3fcaf7-6ccd-5abb-bed1-8fe2a55d99e6" "answer-a7f3918c-bbd9-5833-a7a6-c082875137c2" "answer-474f548f-3852-5cbc-8cd8-8a2e695ea1c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90a38e10-7f75-5d58-827d-ea0f8b66ba3d" :answer/id #uuid "90a38e10-7f75-5d58-827d-ea0f8b66ba3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af7e026a-25c7-5309-a590-6ae712847280" :answer/id #uuid "af7e026a-25c7-5309-a590-6ae712847280" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P(2.5\\le Y\\le 6.5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc3fcaf7-6ccd-5abb-bed1-8fe2a55d99e6" :answer/id #uuid "bc3fcaf7-6ccd-5abb-bed1-8fe2a55d99e6" :answer/type :an